254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (This project successfully demonstrated a complete data science workflow for network intrusion detection using the NSL-KDD Dataset. By leveraging Apache Spark, we efficiently processed data in a distributed environment and built multiple machine learning models, including Random Forest and Isolation Forest. The results showed that machine learning can effectively identify malicious network traffic, while anomaly detection helps in identifying unknown attacks. Overall, the project highlights the importance of scalable data processing and intelligent models in enhancing cybersecurity systems.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
